{"decision":"PROPOSE","invalid_operation":null,"observations":["The cost of a representation is the sum of its digits.","Option 1 cost is the decimal digit sum of n.","Option 2 cost is the binary digit sum (popcount) of n.","We need the largest n < 1000 with decimal digit sum equal to binary digit sum."],"parameter_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"base_a":{"default":10,"description":"First representation base for digit-sum comparison.","minimum":2,"type":"integer"},"base_b":{"default":2,"description":"Second representation base for digit-sum comparison.","minimum":2,"type":"integer"},"hi":{"description":"Exclusive upper bound of the search range.","type":"integer"},"lo":{"description":"Inclusive lower bound of the search range.","type":"integer"},"none_sentinel":{"default":-1,"description":"Value returned if no integer in range satisfies equality.","type":"integer"}},"required":["lo","hi"],"type":"object"},"procedure_plan":"Define a deterministic search over integers in a given range [lo, hi). For each integer n, compute decimal digit sum by repeatedly taking n mod 10 and integer-dividing by 10, and compute binary digit sum by repeatedly taking n mod 2 and integer-dividing by 2. Track the maximum n for which the two sums are equal. Return that maximum, or a sentinel (e.g., null) if none exists. Parameterize by lo, hi, and optionally a base pair (decimal base 10 and binary base 2) so the computation is reusable for analogous digit-sum equality problems.","replacement_operation":null,"source_parameters":{"base_a":10,"base_b":2,"hi":1000,"lo":1,"none_sentinel":-1},"uncertainty":"The plan assumes the intended interpretation is strict inequality n < hi and positive integers; if the range includes 0 or negative values, behavior should be defined by the caller. The sentinel for no solution must be specified."}